{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/945725-what-is-your-favorite-cosmology","id":945725,"title":"What is Your Favorite Cosmology?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-07T16:04:08-07:00","id":945725,"title":"What is Your Favorite Cosmology?","content":"I am just curious about everyone's favorite cosmology and how 'correct' you think that each cosmology is? I will get it started. My favorite is the Fera cosmology from Werewolf, followed by the Kuei-jin cosmology from Kindred of the East.<br /> <br /> I rate the cosmological accuracy in order of most accurate to least accurate by gameline: Werewolf (50%), Kindred of the East (50%), Changeling (25%), Mage (25%), Wraith (10%), Vampire (10%), and Demon (10%).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T21:44:13-07:00","id":945941,"title":"","content":"I default to Werewolf/Mage. They're really not that different (especially from an in game character perspective). Most choices on how the cosmology works will never been seen by players anyways. <br /> <br /> That being said, what matters more is which game I'm running/playing. If I'm running a Vampire game, then the greater cosmology of the universe almost never matters since Vampires don't regularly deal with other worlds so they cease to exist for all intents and purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T22:43:48-07:00","id":945961,"title":"","content":"I'm a fan of assuming that every type of supernatural doesn't actually have a handle on the setting's Cosmology. Every one of them is collectively looking through a keyhole and trying to sort everything out based on the variables of their experiences and assemble a world view that makes sense. All the assorted Cosmologies are correct, but all of them are also incomplete. If someone could step far enough back so they could see the whole picture and all the spaces between the pieces it would make sense, but doing so rockets you out of PC-hood loooong before you get to that point. Games for where there is a 'Transcendence' endgame are the first steps to that goal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T06:54:02-07:00","id":946125,"title":"","content":"I am very Mage in this aspect: Your Cosmology is real (whatever you choose to make to your cosmology).<br /> There is no objective truth","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T18:50:39-07:00","id":946637,"title":"","content":"Mage and Werewolf, mostly because their cosmologies include the Umbra which vastly expands the setting. Wraith is a distant third--though it's more limited, the Underworld is wonderfully detailed. Changelings have The Dreaming... I really like Vampire, but it sucks that you're just stuck in Dallas or Denver or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T19:42:06-07:00","id":946683,"title":"","content":"Changeling and Mage.<br /> <br /> Human thought gives context to the Spirit World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T10:47:46-07:00","id":952609,"title":"","content":"Mage, Werewolf and Wraith all kind of complement each other, covering different parts of the World of Darkness, but being mostly consistent. KotE, likewise, seems to present the same model for the universe, but simplifies it into Yang World, Yin World and Yomi. <br /> <br /> The system of Celestines, Incarna, etc, also allows for Vampire's cosmology (there are so many gods, having YHWH exist doesn't contradict that, and Revelations of the Dark Mother is particularly crossover-friendly with the Mage cosmology).<br /> <br /> Demons can mostly be rationalised as delusional servants of YHWH, and lesser gods with some similarities to humans but without their free will (read: Enlightened Will). Perhaps they're twisted, mutated or else otherwise more primal forms of Avatar wrapped in celestial bodies. They could be the Psychopomps or at least be related to them. Most likely they are or contain fragments of The One, like humanity is or does, and affect the world through these God-shards (Avatars), but without the free will humans have to truly Awaken. They could very well be the lesser Pure Ones, or the Elohim of RotDM. But, being closer to YHWH (who seems to be a higher Pure One, although probably not The One) than humans, they seem more bound up in what he is and what he believes than humans are. <br /> <br /> Humans, ironically, by being further removed from YHWH, seem to have more potential to equal or exceed his own power (e.g., as Lilith did, compared to the relative failure of Lucifer to truly become a god in the same way). Perhaps it's because gods will always, in this cosmology, be servants and slaves to the fragments of The One they serve or are created by (The One being, in this case, Adam Kadmon/Cosmic Man and not some separate supernal entity at all). If this is true, humanity is really God, and all the other gods are created by/imagined by humanity, rather than the other way around. These delusions just keep their true God from realising its true nature. <br /> <br /> Changelings still fit into this cosmology rather well. The Dreaming still exists in the Umbra, except it cuts across multiple layers of it. The only problem with changelings is that they don't realise they fit so neatly into this cosmology. To them, everything else fits into their own conception of the Dreaming as central. In that respect, they're very much like Demons. Like Demons, they can potentially have great power in their true forms, but they're also too inextricably bound up with their god/uber-Avatar/Pure One (in this case the Dreaming) to truly Awaken.<br /> <br /> The Neverborn, as they exist in Wraith and Mage, seem like the anti-Pure Ones. Fragments of The Other that stands against The One. The Qlippoth to the Sephiroth. Oblivion to Prime. Undoing to Becoming. And the fact that The One is fragmented, divided, spread far and wide gives them the balance of power at the moment, as the World of Darkness is leaning towards Entropy more than Dynamism. But when the Time of Judgement comes, the rift between The One and The Other may be healed as The One is devoured by The Other. Thus, it all starts again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 10-03-2016, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T13:34:42-07:00","id":952713,"title":"","content":"Add another vote for Fera's.. Mostly cause that is the setting i spend over half of the time running games for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T14:43:30-07:00","id":952747,"title":"","content":"I generally have more fun with it, especially with the non-Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T15:21:43-07:00","id":952782,"title":"","content":"In my cosmology, the Triat are the oldest entities in the universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T18:01:45-07:00","id":952891,"title":"","content":"I like the mage cosmology because then there are no definitively &quot;wrong&quot; answers. just a lot of half understood truths given very literal form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T00:52:01-07:00","id":980635,"title":"","content":"I prefer the vampire cosmology. Because other than Noddist cults, you have cults for all existing cosmologies in WoD.<br /> <br /> So you can choose whether to believe in Noddism, consensual reality, Gaia and Triat, Yahweh etc...or you can choose to believe in none or all of them, without it having a collective impact.<br /> <br /> I feel it gives the characters the feeling that their belief is free and personal rather than forced on them by some arbitrary truth, like what is the case in other splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 10-03-2016, 04:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T06:58:28-07:00","id":980751,"title":"","content":"I would rather to get the part I like and mixing all to create my own mash-up, and even adding ideas from another no-White Wolf's games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}